        <!-- ==================================================
             H3.2 — THE CITIZEN PROBLEM
             ================================================== -->

        <section
            id="citizen-problem"
            aria-labelledby="citizen-problem-title"
        >

            <div class="container">

                <p>THE CITIZEN PROBLEM</p>

                <h2 id="citizen-problem-title">
                    Public systems are often difficult to navigate.
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Citizens may know what is wrong but still struggle to
                    identify the responsible institution, understand the
                    relevant process, or determine what action should come
                    next.
                </p>

                <div>

                    <article>
                        <h3>Unclear Responsibility</h3>
                        <p>
                            It can be difficult to identify which office,
                            institution, or authority is responsible.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <h3>Complex Processes</h3>
                        <p>
                            Rules, procedures, documents, and administrative
                            pathways can be difficult to understand.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <h3>Weak Feedback Loops</h3>
                        <p>
                            Citizens may not know whether an issue was
                            received, acted upon, or resolved.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- ==================================================
             H3.3 — WHAT JANAVANI IS
             ================================================== -->

        <section
            id="what-is-janavani"
            aria-labelledby="what-is-janavani-title"
        >

            <div class="container">

                <p>WHAT IS JANAVANI?</p>

                <h2 id="what-is-janavani-title">
                    A civic intelligence layer between citizens
                    and public systems.
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Janavani is designed to help transform a citizen's
                    experience from confusion into a structured pathway:
                    understand the issue, identify the relevant system,
                    navigate the process, and participate in accountability.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- ==================================================
             H3.4 — CITIZEN PATHWAY
             ================================================== -->

        <section
            id="citizen-pathway"
            aria-labelledby="citizen-pathway-title"
        >

            <div class="container">

                <p>THE JANAVANI PATHWAY</p>

                <h2 id="citizen-pathway-title">
                    From a citizen's concern to a structured civic pathway.
                </h2>

                <div>

                    <article>
                        <span>01</span>
                        <h3>Describe</h3>
                        <p>
                            Describe the public problem in ordinary language.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <span>02</span>
                        <h3>Understand</h3>
                        <p>
                            Understand the relevant system, responsibility,
                            and available pathway.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <span>03</span>
                        <h3>Navigate</h3>
                        <p>
                            Identify the appropriate office, process,
                            documents, or next action.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <span>04</span>
                        <h3>Participate</h3>
                        <p>
                            Participate in improving public systems through
                            informed civic action.
                        </p>
                    </article>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- ==================================================
             H3.5 — VIGILANCE & ACCOUNTABILITY
             ================================================== -->

        <section
            id="vigilance-accountability"
            aria-labelledby="vigilance-title"
        >

            <div class="container">

                <p>VIGILANCE &amp; ACCOUNTABILITY</p>

                <h2 id="vigilance-title">
                    Better information creates stronger accountability.
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Janavani aims to make public-system interactions more
                    transparent by helping citizens understand responsibility,
                    process, status, and the institutional pathways available
                    to them.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- ==================================================
             H3.6 — CITIZEN PARTICIPATION
             ================================================== -->

        <section
            id="citizen-participation"
            aria-labelledby="participation-title"
        >

            <div class="container">

                <p>CITIZEN PARTICIPATION</p>

                <h2 id="participation-title">
                    Governance improves when citizens can participate
                    meaningfully.
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Janavani is intended not only to help citizens resolve
                    individual problems, but also to create pathways for
                    learning, feedback, participation, and systemic
                    improvement.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


